# Ignore Files

# Reverse-engineering working files. The Ghidra project regenerates from the
# local SOVIET64.exe in minutes, so it is not worth versioning.
ghidra/

# Build output. tesmiolauncher.exe, tesmioloader.dll and plugins\*.dll all land
# here, along with the live tesmioloader.ini the launcher writes.
build/

# btfconvert has its own build.bat and does not go through build\ at all: it
# writes its objects to btfconvert\obj\ and the exe beside its own source.
btfconvert/obj/
btfconvert/btfconvert.exe

# The Python helpers docs/ refers to (tools/pe/*.py, tools/assets/*.py) and the
# signing key under tools/signing/. See docs/03-reverse-engineering.md on what
# is and is not in this repository, and why nothing is lost by it.
tools/
tsmsign.obj

# The signing machinery, neither half of which is in this fork. The public half,
# src/tesmio_pubkey.h, is exactly what ships - it is compiled into the launcher
# so it can verify; the half that must never ship is the private key,
# tools/signing/tsm_private.bin, ignored above. src/tesmio_sign.h is the code
# both sides include. The ignore is here so a checkout synced with upstream does
# not stage either file back in. Without them the launcher builds fine and
# simply never mentions signatures - see the __has_include block in
# src/tesmiolauncher.cpp.
src/tesmio_pubkey.h
src/tesmio_sign.h

# Notes
идеи.txt
